<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waroch II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 577–594</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Waroch, Guerech</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Waroch II was a Breton count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vannes">Vannes</a> in the late 6th century, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macliau">Macliau</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory of Tours</a> he repeatedly raided the Frankish territories around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a> and defeated or bought off Frankish armies sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilperic-i">Chilperic I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guntram">Guntram</a>. The region of Vannes came to be called Bro Waroch, or Broërec, after him.</p></div>
